Original PARSIFAL sources
Copyright (c) Mitchell P. Marcus

The files in this directory (notes/from-marcus/) are the original PARSIFAL
sources, written by Mitchell P. Marcus while a graduate student at MIT.
They are reproduced here verbatim and used with his written permission
(email to Bruce Seely, June 2026). Mitchell Marcus retains full copyright;
to his knowledge no other party (e.g. AT&T/Bell Labs) holds rights in these
files.

These files are made available under the following terms, granted by the
author:

  PERMISSION. You may freely use, redistribute, and modify these sources,
  including modifying them as required to get them running under another
  language (as the Common Lisp port in the parent repository does).

  CONDITION. You may NOT modify these sources and then redistribute them as
  if they were the original. If you distribute or run a modified version,
  you must make clear that it has been changed and is not Mitchell Marcus's
  original source. The author makes specific claims about PARSIFAL's
  behavior in his published work and asks that any program represented as
  PARSIFAL continue to meet those claims.

These terms apply to the source files Mitchell Marcus authored. The grammar
appendix reproduced (OCR'd) elsewhere in this project is drawn from his book
"A Theory of Syntactic Recognition for Natural Language" (MIT Press, 1980);
any rights in that published text are a separate matter from this grant.

